{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":3078,"output":7720,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":5801,"totalTokens":10798,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Let me review each item.\n\nQ041: \"Accept these selections\" → \"确认法术选择\". Source has no \"法术\" (spell). Target adds spell selection; \"these selections\" = 这些选择. \"确认法术选择\" adds 法术. That's ADDITION — but rule 3: new info compatible with visible evidence and cannot be contradicted... Context likely spell selection. Hmm, \"Accept these selections\" — target omits \"these\" and adds 法术. The addition of 法术 cannot be verified from visible evidence. Rule 3 says additions compatible with evidence that cannot be judged wrong don't count. But \"these selections\" → \"法术选择\" changes demonstrative \"these\" to specific \"spell\". This could be a FINDING for ADDITION/OMISSION: target omits \"these\" and adds \"法术\" without evidence. I'd report as UNCERTAIN or FINDING. The source alone doesn't mention spells; the addition is a substantive change but could come from context not visible. Rule 3 says don't report. But the omission of \"these\"... Hmm. I'll report FINDING ADDITION: 法术 not supported; also \"these selections\" vs \"法术选择\". Actually safer: FINDING? The rule 3 explicitly protects compatible additions. Adding \"法术\" is compatible (selections could be spells). Cannot be judged wrong by visible evidence. So per rule 3, not a defect. But the demonstrative \"these\" is dropped — that's a subtle omission. Hmm, \"确认这些选择\" would be literal. Dropping \"these\" — the target still conveys accept selections. I'll leave empty or report UNCERTAIN. I'll leave candidates empty with observation noting it.\n\nQ042: \"Got to level 10 of the infinite dungeon.\" → \"到达无尽地下城第10层。\" Correct.\n\nQ043: \"THAT'S NOT A VERY HERMIT-LIKE ATTITUDE.\" → \"这可不像我这个隐士该有的态度。\" Source \"that's\" refers to some attitude; target says \"我这个隐士\" — adds 我 (my hermit-like attitude). Subject shift: source \"that's not a very hermit-like attitude\" — could be speaker saying to someone. Target \"我这个隐士\" claims the speaker is the hermit. Could be speaker commenting on another's action. This is a SUBJECT/REFERENT issue. Without context, the speaker could be the hermit. Source doesn't say whose attitude. Target adds 我. Rule 3? The addition \"我\" cannot be judged wrong by visible evidence... but it changes referent. Hmm. \"THAT'S NOT A VERY HERMIT-LIKE ATTITUDE\" — the hermit could be the addressee. Target specifies \"我这个隐士\" which asserts speaker is the hermit. This is a REFERENT determination not supported. I'd say UNCERTAIN. Actually, in game context (ToME), this is from the Temporal Wardens or... Actually this line is in ToME said by... \"hermit\" — likely the player is the hermit? Unknown. I'll mark UNCERTAIN REFERENT: target asserts speaker is the hermit; source only says the attitude is not hermit-like without specifying whose.\n\nQ044: \"Have 100 walls on the sludgenest turn into hostile creatures.\" → \"让淤泥巢穴中的 200 面墙变成敌对生物。\" 100 vs 200 — clear VALUE FINDING.\n\nQ045: \"But what is all th...\" → \"但是这一切到底是……\" Fine (truncated). OK.\n\nQ046: \"Killed a Bringer of Doom.\" → \"杀死一名厄运行者。\" \"Bringer of Doom\" → \"厄运行者\" — a translation choice; \"bringer of doom\" = 厄运带来者. \"厄运行者\" is a name translation. Acceptable? \"Bringer of Doom\" as achievement name. 厄运行者 conveys it roughly. Not a defect per rules. Empty.\n\nQ047: Long text. Source: \"ruined from your fight with the creature carrying it\" → \"看来在你刚才和那个人类搏斗的时候被打碎了\" — \"the creature carrying it\" (the creature carrying the paper) → \"那个人类\" (that human). Source says \"creature\", target says \"人类\" (human). Later text mentions 'sun paladin' species — sun paladins are human. Hmm, \"creature\" → \"human\" adds specificity. Also \"ruined\" (毁坏) → \"被打碎\" (shattered). Minor. Also source: \"next step of emigration program should be cleaning of local 'sun paladin' nest and establishment of...\" → target: \"移民计划的下一步是清理本地的\"太阳骑士\"巢穴并建立…\" — \"should be\" (应当是) → target states it as fact without 应当. Modality omission: \"should be\" vs 是. That's a CONDITION/modality change. FINDING? The quote says \"should be cleaning... and establishment of...\" Target: \"移民计划的下一步是清理…并建立…\" — drops \"should\". This changes a recommendation to a statement. I'd report FINDING OMISSION of \"should\" — or STATE. Hmm, it's modality. CLAIM type: CONDITION or STATE. I'll report as FINDING, claim_type CONDITION, target_span \"移民计划的下一步是清理本地的“太阳骑士”巢穴并建立\", correction \"移民计划的下一步应当是清理本地的“太阳骑士”巢穴并建立\", evidence \"next step of emigration program should be cleaning\".\n\nAlso \"creature carrying it\" → \"那个人类\": SPECIES unspecified vs human. Since later text says sun paladin species, human is compatible and can't be judged wrong... Actually the creature carrying the scraps — the fight with \"the creature carrying it\" — in game it's a sun paladin (human). But rule 1: only visible evidence. The visible text mentions species 'sun paladin' but doesn't say humans. \"Creature\" is generic; \"human\" is a specification that can't be judged wrong from visible text? Well \"creature\" doesn't contradict human. Rule 3 protects it. Skip.\n\nAlso \"you can piece some of it together to read\" — fine.\n\nAlso \"ruined from your fight\" → \"被打碎了\" — fine.\n\nQ048: \"Records of Lorekeeper Hadak part three\" → \"博学者哈达克的记录，第三部分\" Fine.\n\nQ049: \"When you do a mouse gesture (right click + drag) a color coded trail is displayed.\" → \"当你用右键拖动画出鼠标手势时，始终会显示彩色的轨迹提示。\" Source: conditional \"when you do... a trail is displayed\". Target adds \"始终\" (always). That changes conditional to unconditional. FINDING: ADDITION \"始终\". Evidence: \"When you do a mouse gesture ... a trail is displayed\". Target span \"始终会显示\". FINDING ADDITION.\n\nQ050: Long. Source: \"(You see here a large, elaborate fountain.\" Target adds \"位于德斯镇\" (located in Derth) — addition not in source. That's ADDITION of location. Rule 3: compatible? The fountain... cannot be judged wrong by visible evidence. Hmm. Rule 3 protects it. But it's substantive added info. Rule 3 says don't report. Skip.\n\nCarvings: \"ALL ARE WELCOME WHO LEARN FROM THE MISTAKES OF THE PAST\" → \"欢迎所有从过去的错误中吸取教训之人\" fine.\n\n\"LET THE ARCANE ONCE MORE BE A BOON AND NOT A BANE TO MAJ'EYAL\" → \"愿奥术再度成为马基·埃亚尔的助益，而非灾祸\" — \"LET\" imperative → \"愿\" (may). Minor, acceptable. Fine.\n\n\"MAY WE HAVE THE WISDOM TO ONE DAY REUNITE THE WORLD IN SAFETY AND ENLIGHTENMENT\" → fine.\n\n\"GATHER HERE IN PEACE TO DISCOVER AND PERFECT THE KNOWLEDGE OF HOW, AND WHEN, TO WEAVE THE WORLD'S FABRIC\" → \"在此和平相聚，探索并完善何时、如何编织世界织物的知识\" — fine, order swapped acceptable.\n\n\"around the outside of the fountain stand statues of...\" → \"喷泉外缘周围站着几座雕像\" fine. \"a statue of Linaniil stands in the center\" fine.\n\n\"The runes and the fireball are not connected to anything, and float in a fixed position in the air.\" → \"那些符文与火球未与任何东西相连，却保持在空中的固定位置。\" fine.\n\n\"her arms outstretched to welcome all\" fine.\n\nQ051: \"If you bring me a gem and a ring, I can create a new ring imbued with the properties of the gem.\" → \"如果你给我找来一颗宝石和一枚项链，我可以帮你把宝石的力量镶嵌到戒指里去。\" — \"a ring\" → \"项链\" (necklace/amulet)! Ring = 戒指, 项链 = necklace. Clear VALUE FINDING. Target span \"一枚项链\", correction \"一枚戒指\", evidence \"a gem and a ring\".\n\nAlso \"The original traits of the ring will be lost\" → \"这颗戒指里面原来所有的属性会丢失掉\" fine.\n\n\"There is a small fee dependent on the level of the ring, and you need a quality ring to use a quality gem.\" → \"不过根据戒指等级我要收取一小笔费用。你得寻找高品质的戒指来用于高品质的宝石。\" fine-ish.\n\nAlso \"expert jeweler\" → \"珠宝专家\" fine.\n\nQ052: \"But then where are they now if they won?\" → \"兽人是胜利了，但是现在他们又在哪里呢？\" Adds \"兽人\" (orcs) — \"they\" unspecified. Addition of 兽人 not supported by visible source. Rule 3: compatible? Can't be judged wrong from visible text... \"they\" could be orcs. Protected by rule 3? Hmm, rule 3 covers \"新增但与可见证据相容、且无法由可见证据判错的具体信息\". Adding 兽人 — visible evidence doesn't identify \"they\", so can't judge wrong. Skip. But it also restructures \"But then where are they now if they won?\" → \"兽人是胜利了，但是现在他们又在哪里呢？\" preserving meaning. Fine.\n\nQ053: \"Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared.\" → \"几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了。\" Tense: \"I'll have everything prepared\" future → \"准备好了\" could be read as already. \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" — Chinese ambiguity; likely read as future result. Fine-ish. \"If you happen to find a text ... return with it and your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\" → \"请帮我带回来\" — source \"return with it\" (bring it back with you when you return) — target \"请帮我带回来\" fine. \"It opens the ruins of Telmur, which the men of Sholtar sealed many years ago.\" → \"它可以打开泰尔玛废墟，那是多年前肖尔塔人封印的地方。\" — \"the men of Sholtar\" → \"肖尔塔人\" fine. OK.\n\nActually \"几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了\" — hmm \"I'll have everything prepared\" = will have prepared. Fine.\n\nQ054: \"I cleared the room of death and all I got was this lousy achievement!\" → \"我清完“死亡之屋”后发现我只得到了这个无聊的成就！\" Fine.\n\nQ055: \"The Right thing to do\" → \"放走鲜血大师才是正确的选择\". Adds \"放走鲜血大师\" (release the Bloodmaster) — addition not in source. Title of achievement. Rule 3: can't judge wrong from visible evidence? The source title is vague; target specifies action. Compatible. Skip per rule 3. Hmm but it's a substantive specification... I'll skip.\n\nQ056: Long narrative. Source: \"realizing it's actually a human inside that hulking, worn armor.\" → \"才发现那副庞大而破旧的战甲里其实装着弗莉吉亚的弟弟。\" — \"a human\" → \"弗莉吉亚的弟弟\" (Fligia's younger brother?). That's a big addition. Source says \"a human\". Target specifies identity. Rule 3: compatible with visible evidence? Source doesn't mention 弗莉吉亚. Can't be judged wrong from visible text... but it's a specific identity addition. Rule 3 literally protects it since visible evidence doesn't contradict. Hmm. But is it \"相容\"? Yes — a human could be Fligia's brother. Per rule 3, skip. But this feels like it deserves scrutiny... The rules say only report what visible text supports. The addition of \"弗莉吉亚的弟弟\" cannot be judged wrong. I'll skip per rule 3, or mention in observation.\n\n\"f...t...ma....ll...\" → \"弗……特……玛……尔……\" — transliteration: f-t-ma-ll. Target has 弗(f)特(t)玛(ma)尔(l?) — \"ll\" → 尔. Hmm \"ma....ll\" — \"尔\" for \"ll\"? 4 syllables: f, t, ma, ll. Target: 弗, 特, 玛, 尔 — 4 chars. OK roughly.\n\n\"You hear a devilish voice, coming from everywhere at once!!\" → fine.\n\n\"Then you are at the right place\" — that's Q051.\n\n\"unable to understand anything! It doesn't seem like any language used in Maj'Eyal!\" → \"你完全听不懂！这不像马基·埃亚尔使用的任何一种语言！\" fine.\n\nAlso \"Standing right before you, a massive battle armor with an equally massive battle axe.\" → \"一副同样手持巨大战斧的巨型战甲，就站在你面前。\" — \"an equally massive battle axe\" means the axe is equally massive as the armor. Target: \"同样手持巨大战斧\" — \"同样\" misplaced; reads as \"equally holding a huge battle axe\". Meaning roughly preserved? Source: armor equally massive as its axe. Target: 同样 modifies 手持. Hmm, minor. Could be FINDING? \"equally massive\" describes the axe's mass relative to armor. Target \"同样手持巨大战斧的巨型战甲\" — ambiguous, loses \"equally massive\" for axe. I might report UNCERTAIN. Actually \"一副同样手持巨大战斧\" — 同样 likely modifies the whole: \"likewise holding\" (i.e., it too holds an axe). Source means the axe is as massive as the armor. The target loses that comparison. I'd report FINDING? It's a STATE/VALUE nuance. I'll report UNCERTAIN with correction \"手持一把同样巨大的战斧的巨型战甲\". Evidence \"an equally massive battle axe\".\n\nAlso \"a massive battle armor\" → \"巨型战甲\" fine. \"It wasn't there just a second ago.\" → \"一瞬之前那里还空无一物。\" fine.\n\n\"your rival\" → \"自己的对手\" fine.\n\nQ057: \"Reload/regenerate Zone and level\" → \"重新加载/重新生成地图和角色\" — \"level\" → \"角色\"? Zone and level → 地图和角色. \"level\" here is game level/层级, not character. FINDING: VALUE. Correction: \"重新加载/重新生成区域和层级\". Evidence \"Zone and level\". Target span \"地图和角色\". FINDING.\n\nQ058: \"Lua inspect [Projectile]\" → \"即使此处没有抛射物，也可在 Lua 中查看 [抛射物]\" — adds \"即使此处没有抛射物，也\" — big addition. Not supported. Rule 3: compatible? It's debug tool text; the addition can't be judged wrong... but the source is just a label \"Lua inspect [Projectile]\". The addition is substantive. Rule 3 protects incompatible additions only if judged wrong. Hmm, additions that change meaning: \"Lua inspect [Projectile]\" is a menu label meaning \"inspect [Projectile] in Lua\". Target says \"even if there's no projectile here, you can inspect [Projectile] in Lua\". This adds a conditional claim. Can visible evidence judge it wrong? The source doesn't say that. It's unsupported addition. Rule 3 says additions compatible with visible evidence AND cannot be judged wrong by visible evidence don't count. This addition can't be judged wrong... but it changes the meaning of the string substantially. I think this is the kind of case where the addition is clearly not derivable and the instruction's rule 3 is meant to protect plausible contextual additions. Hmm. A debug option label with a long explanatory clause — the addition is a whole different sentence. I'd report FINDING ADDITION: target_span \"即使此处没有抛射物，也\", correction \"Lua 查看 [抛射物]\", evidence \"Lua inspect [Projectile]\". Actually I'm torn. Rule 3: \"新增但与可见证据相容、且无法由可见证据判错的具体信息\". \"即使此处没有抛射物\" — can visible evidence judge it wrong? The source is a label; the addition claims behavior not stated. I'd argue visible evidence (source text) doesn't support it and the label meaning is changed — the target is no longer a translation of the label. I'll report FINDING ADDITION.\n\nQ059: \"Removed 89 beneficial effects from enemies via Disintegration.\" → \"必须单次使用裂解清除敌人身上的89个增益效果\" — source is a stat/log statement (past: removed 89). Target turns it into a requirement: \"必须单次\" (must in a single use). Source doesn't say single use or requirement. Big ADDITION/DIRECTION. Source is declarative past-tense record; target is a requirement with \"必须单次\" not in source. FINDING: target_span \"必须单次\", claim ACTION or ADDITION. Also source \"89\" preserved. Report FINDING ADDITION: \"必须单次使用裂解清除\" — source only states fact of removal. Correction: \"通过裂解清除了敌人身上的89个增益效果\". Evidence: \"Removed 89 beneficial effects from enemies via Disintegration.\" Claim type: ADDITION (adds 必须单次 requirement). FINDING.\n\nQ060: \"Killed oneself as a halfling.\" → \"选择半身人种族并杀死敌人。\" — Source: killed oneself (suicide) as a halfling. Target: choose halfling race and kill enemies — direction reversed! FINDING DIRECTION: target_span \"杀死敌人\", correction \"自杀/杀死自己\", evidence \"Killed oneself\". FINDING.\n\nNow back to Q041. \"Accept these selections\" → \"确认法术选择\". Decide: report or not. The omission of \"these\" and addition of 法术. In ToME, this is the character creation point-buy \"Accept these selections\" for talent/category points? Actually \"Accept these selections\" appears in levelup dialog for accepting point selections. \"法术选择\" adds spell. Hmm, in the world of ToME, could be any selection. The target changes \"these selections\" to \"spell selections\" — a specification. Rule 3 protects if can't be judged wrong. The demonstrative \"these\" dropped — meaning shift from \"accept these (current) selections\" to \"confirm spell selection\". I'll report UNCERTAIN? Actually, the core meaning \"accept\" → \"确认\" fine. The addition of 法术 is the issue. I'll add UNCERTAIN ADDITION for \"法术\". Hmm, or skip. The safest per rules: rule 3 protects. But \"these\" omission: the target doesn't convey \"these [current] selections\". I'll report one candidate: UNCERTAIN, ADDITION, span \"法术\", correction \"这些\", evidence \"Accept these selections\". Hmm — is it FINDING? Without context, whether selections are spells can't be determined. I'll use UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ043: decide UNCERTAIN REFERENT for \"我这个隐士\". Evidence \"THAT'S NOT A VERY HERMIT-LIKE ATTITUDE.\" Correction: \"这可不太像隐士该有的态度。\"\n\nQ047: also \"you can piece some of it together to read\" → \"你只能依稀拼凑出一些文字\" fine. \"ineffective on species 'sun paladin'\" → \"在'太阳骑士'这种物种的身上被证明无效\" — \"proven ineffective\"? Source: \"pheromone signals effective on much Eyalite wildlife ineffective on species 'sun paladin'.\" Target adds \"被证明\" (proven) — minor, fine. \"much Eyalite wildlife\" → \"大部分埃亚尔野生生命体\" fine.\n\nAlso Q047: \"ruined from your fight with the creature carrying it\" → \"在你刚才和那个人类搏斗的时候被打碎了\" — \"creature\" → \"人类\". Should I report? Rule 3 protects since sun paladin (human) is mentioned later in the same text — actually the visible text mentions species 'sun paladin', and the creature carried the note about sun paladins. Compatible. Skip.\n\nQ050: \"位于德斯镇\" addition — skip per rule 3. Hmm, or report? The visible source says \"(You see here a large, elaborate fountain.\" No location. Adding 德斯镇 — can visible evidence judge wrong? No. Skip per rule 3. I'll note in observation.\n\nQ056: also \"You look around searching for your rival\" — fine. Also line \"a massive battle armor with an equally massive battle axe\" — I decided UNCERTAIN. Also the 弗莉吉亚的弟弟 addition — skip per rule 3 (mention in observation).\n\nHmm wait — should I report the 弟弟 addition? The instruction says only objective defects supportable by visible text. The addition of a named character's identity is a classic hallucination-like addition but rule 3 explicitly shields compatible additions. I'll mention in observation without candidate.\n\nQ052: 兽人 addition — skip, note in observation.\n\nQ055: skip, note in observation.\n\nNow Q049: \"When you do a mouse gesture (right click + drag) a color coded trail is displayed.\" → \"始终会显示\" — FINDING ADDITION of 始终. Yes.\n\nAlso \"color coded trail\" → \"彩色的轨迹提示\" — \"color coded\" = 颜色编码的, 彩色 is close enough. Fine.\n\nQ053: check \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\" → \"这能大大提高你通过传送门时存活的几率\" — \"our portal attempt\" → \"通过传送门\" fine. OK.\n\nQ051: also \"The original traits of the ring will be lost in the process but new ones of similar quality will be generated.\" → \"这颗戒指里面原来所有的属性会丢失掉，不过也会生成一些质量相似的新属性。\" fine.\n\nAlso Q051: \"There is a small fee dependent on the level of the ring\" → \"根据戒指等级我要收取一小笔费用\" fine.\n\nOne candidate for Q051 (项链→戒指). Wait, also \"If you bring me a gem and a ring, I can create a new ring imbued with the properties of the gem.\" Target: \"我可以帮你把宝石的力量镶嵌到戒指里去\" — means create a new ring; roughly fine.\n\nQ057: FINDING.\n\nQ058: FINDING ADDITION.\n\nQ059: FINDING ADDITION (\"必须单次\" requirement not in source). Also could be VALUE? No, just addition of condition. claim_type ADDITION. Actually also the source is past tense record; target imperative requirement — ACTION/OTHER. I'll do ADDITION with correction.\n\nQ060: FINDING DIRECTION.\n\nQ044: FINDING VALUE.\n\nNow count candidates:\n- Q041: 1 UNCERTAIN (法术 addition / these omission)\n- Q042: empty\n- Q043: 1 UNCERTAIN REFERENT\n- Q044: 1 FINDING VALUE\n- Q045: empty\n- Q046: empty\n- Q047: 1 FINDING (should omission → modality). claim_type: CONDITION? \"should be\" modality — I'll use CONDITION. Or STATE. I'll use CONDITION.\n- Q048: empty\n- Q049: 1 FINDING ADDITION (始终)\n- Q050: empty\n- Q051: 1 FINDING VALUE (项链)\n- Q052: empty\n- Q053: empty\n- Q054: empty\n- Q055: empty\n- Q056: 1 UNCERTAIN (equally massive)\n- Q057: 1 FINDING VALUE\n- Q058: 1 FINDING ADDITION\n- Q059: 1 FINDING ADDITION\n- Q060: 1 FINDING DIRECTION\n\nQ041 target_span must be verbatim: \"法术\". Evidence verbatim from source: \"Accept these selections\". Correction: \"确认这些选择\". Claim ADDITION.\n\nQ043 span: \"我这个隐士\". Evidence: \"THAT'S NOT A VERY HERMIT-LIKE ATTITUDE.\"\n\nQ044 span: \"200 面墙\". Correction: \"100 面墙\". Evidence: \"Have 100 walls on the sludgenest\".\n\nQ047 span: \"移民计划的下一步是清理本地的\"太阳骑士\"巢穴并建立\" — must be verbatim including quotes: target uses “太阳骑士”. Verbatim: 移民计划的下一步是清理本地的“太阳骑士”巢穴并建立. Correction: 移民计划的下一步应当是清理本地的“太阳骑士”巢穴并建立. Evidence: \"next step of emigration program should be cleaning\".\n\nQ049 span: \"始终会显示\". Correction: \"会显示\". Evidence: \"When you do a mouse gesture (right click + drag) a color coded trail is displayed\".\n\nQ051 span: \"一枚项链\". Correction: \"一枚戒指\". Evidence: \"bring me a gem and a ring\".\n\nQ056 span: \"同样手持巨大战斧\". Correction: \"手持一把同样巨大的战斧\". Evidence: \"a massive battle armor with an equally massive battle axe\". Verdict UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ057 span: \"地图和角色\". Correction: \"区域和层级\". Evidence: \"Reload/regenerate Zone and level\".\n\nQ058 span: \"即使此处没有抛射物，也\". Correction: \"在 Lua 中查看 [抛射物]\" — hmm correction should fix. Full correction: \"可在 Lua 中查看 [抛射物]\". Evidence: \"Lua inspect [Projectile]\". Verdict FINDING, ADDITION.\n\nQ059 span: \"必须单次使用裂解清除敌人身上的89个增益效果\" — correction: \"通过裂解清除了敌人身上的89个增益效果\". Evidence: \"Removed 89 beneficial effects from enemies via Disintegration.\" FINDING, ADDITION.\n\nQ060 span: \"杀死敌人\". Correction: \"自杀（杀死自己）\". Evidence: \"Killed oneself as a halfling.\" FINDING, DIRECTION.\n\nObservations for each — brief neutral description."}}
