er is the hermit. Could be speaker commenting on another's action. This is a SUBJECT/REFERENT issue. Without context, the speaker could be the hermit. Source doesn't say whose attitude. Target adds 我. Rule 3? The addition \"我\" cannot be judged wrong by visible evidence... but it changes referent. Hmm. \"THAT'S NOT A VERY HERMIT-LIKE ATTITUDE\" — the hermit could be the addressee. Target specifies \"我这个隐士\" which asserts speaker is the hermit. This is a REFERENT determination not supported. I'd say UNCERTAIN. Actually, in game context (ToME), this is from the Temporal Wardens or... Actually this line is in ToME said by... \"hermit\" — likely the player is the hermit? Unknown. I'll mark UNCERTAIN REFERENT: target asserts speaker is the hermit; source only says the attitude is not hermit-like without specifying whose.\n\nQ044: \"Have 100 walls on the sludgenest turn into hostile creatures.\" → \"让淤泥巢穴中的 200 面墙变成敌对生物。\" 100 vs 200 — clear VALUE FINDING.\n\nQ045: \"But what is all th...\" → \"但是这一切到底是……\" Fine (truncated). OK.\n\nQ046: \"Killed a Bringer of Doom.\" → \"杀死一名厄运行者。\" \"Bringer of Doom\" → \"厄运行者\" — a translation choice; \"bringer of doom\" = 厄运带来者. \"厄运行者\" is a name translation. Acceptable? \"Bringer of Doom\" as achievement name. 厄运行者 conveys it roughly. Not a defect per rules. Empty.\n\nQ047: Long text. Source: \"ruined from your fight with the creature carrying it\" → \"看来在你刚才和那个人类搏斗的时候被打碎了\" — \"the creature carrying it\" (the creature carrying the paper) → \"那个人类\" (that human). Source says \"creature\", target says \"人类\" (human). Later text mentions 'sun paladin' species — sun paladins are human. Hmm, \"creature\" → \"human\" adds specificity. Also \"ruined\" (毁坏) → \"被打碎\" (shattered). Minor. Also source: \"next step of emigration program should be cleaning of local 'sun paladin' nest and establishment of...\" → target: \"移民计划的下一步是清理本地的\"太阳骑士\"巢穴并建立…\" — \"should be\" (应当是) → target states it as fact without 应当. Modality omission: \"should be\" v